fy/sparse_energy_7996.py; python/carnot/verify/dependency_scoped_admission_8291.py; results/experiment_8291_v716_dependency_scoped_admission.json; results/experiment_7432_v651_update_placement.json; openspec/capabilities/kan/spec.md; openspec/capabilities/self-learning/spec.md\nTASK:\nQualify exact spline update isolation and durable recovery. Deliver results/experiment_8306_v717_local_update_isolation.json. Create the thin runner scripts/experiments/experiment_8306_v717_local_update_isolation.py. Store primitive evidence under results/raw/experiment_8306_v717_local_update_isolation/. Read current upstream tasks by their exact declared deliverables; paths not yet produced are dependencies, not historical files.\nCONCRETE STEPS:\n1. PRECONDITIONS: Emit a flushed start line. Authenticate input bytes and terminal/adversarial sidecars. Check private scratch, tools and required resources before measurement. Missing external operands produce complete_blocked_<operand>, verdict_class=blocked and exact gate_check_summary; never substitute simulated observations.\n2. Emit a flushed progress line at every phase boundary and before and after every model load, generation, benchmark and subprocess. Print completed/pending counts inside long loops and a heartbeat at least every 60 seconds while children run; keep every gap below 600 seconds. Use unbuffered output, deadlines and owned process-group cleanup. Write any file over about 200 lines in several tool calls of at most about 150 lines, with a progress message between calls. Split commands and file creation into resumable batches; no single huge tool call and no padded runtime.\n3. Spec first: add relevant REQ-* and SCENARIO-* before implementation. Write focused failing tests first. Preserve existing tests, validators and historical primary bytes. Reuse existing numeric and reporting modules through small adapters. Freeze owned validation argv and private fixture paths. Scratch belongs in /tmp; real runners in scripts/experiments/. No generator-weight updates or external publication.\n4. Declare no_model_load, inference_substrate=verifier_ensemble_against_cached_candidates and MODEL_SPECS=[]. Reuse the tested spline basis and V716 complete-closure lesson. Do not rerun the 24-graph Boolean study as new science.\n5. Implement a thin four-input, eight-coefficient-per-input cubic-spline head plus intercept and holistic-logit slope: 34 parameters. Knot vector=[0,0,0,0,.2,.4,.6,.8,1,1,1,1]. Use natural [0,1] feature bounds, stable sigmoid, identical coefficient ordering and eta=a*x[0]+b+sum(theta*B), with slope a trained statically and frozen online. Dense and sparse implementations evaluate the SAME gradient and scalar norm clip; clip coordinates into [-4,4]. No online global weight decay or moving knots: either would invalidate a local-write claim.\n6. Build an exact reverse index from nonzero basis coefficients to registered prediction-cache entries. An intercept or holistic-slope change invalidates every entry; zero changes invalidate none. Missing or stale metadata falls back to full invalidation. Transaction state includes coefficients, index version, pending issued predictions and applied feedback IDs; issued probabilities remain immutable after invalidation.\n7. Test 48 constructed input trajectories: 3 seeds x4 knot-boundary/overlap patterns x4 feedback fault patterns, 64 events each. Compare full scan with indexed invalidation and a deliberately unsafe truncated index. Include duplicate, stale, missing-metadata, coefficient-projection and intercept-changing events. Use finite differences and scalar independently recomputed basis values.\n8. Require max dense/sparse logit and effective-coefficient error <=1e-10, identical typed actions including boundary escalation, zero stale-cache uses and zero double updates. Kill only owned worker children at events24/48 and verify exact semantic resume against uninterrupted state. Negative controls must detect a planted stale-cache decision; oracle fixture success is circular_positive.\n9. Record operation touches and complete issue/release/checkpoint latency for 5 alternating paired repetitions after one warmup, <=600 seconds of measurement. A local basis does not guarantee less invalidation because the intercept is global. Set local_kernel_ready_score only on correctness and recovery, independent of speed. Preserve global invalidation costs even if they eliminate the expected benefit.\n10. Run applicable E2E-020 private hard-exit recovery. Run the specified private E2E checks from ops/e2e-test-plan.md and relevant unit/consumer tests. Require 100 percent newly owned statement coverage including real CLI, child, failure and recovery paths. Run scoped Ruff check/format, strict mypy and scripts/check_spec_coverage.py --files <owned-test-files>. Keep exact argv, exit codes, clocks and output hashes. Use pytest -n 0 -o addopts= with private scratch. Do not launch the full repository test suite inside this bounded experiment.\n11. Cold-replay primitive rows in a fresh process, including valid, negative and rehashed-tamper controls. Validate a private candidate with unchanged primary_publication checks, scripts/adversarial_verify.py --json <private-candidate> and scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py --strict <private-candidate>. Publish the terminal primary atomically after normal completion and required checks. Failed owned checks disqualify and set readiness to zero. External incompleteness is blocked, not partial. Reconcile openspec/, _bmad/traceability.md, ops/status.md and ops/changelog.md. Do not modify research-roadmap.yaml.\nREQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:\nexperiment_id, task_id, milestone, run_date: principle: Identify the actual invocation and its execution authority.\nhonest_verdict, verdict_class: principle: Terminal honest_verdict starts complete_; verdict_class is positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial. Partial is only retryable unfinished owned work, never an unchan