nCLAUDE.md; CODEX.md; ops/e2e-test-plan.md; ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml; openspec/capabilities/research-reporting/spec.md; openspec/capabilities/verification/spec.md; scripts/experiment_template.py; python/carnot/reporting/primary_publication.py; openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-vNEXT.md; python/carnot/verify/sentence_energy_8183.py; python/carnot/verify/sparse_energy_7996.py; results/experiment_8183_v707_sentence_energy_fit.json; results/experiment_7996_v693_sparse_energy_training.json; openspec/capabilities/kan/spec.md\nTASK:\nFit calibrated local sentence energies against matched-information controls. Deliver results/experiment_8308_v717_sentence_spline_fit.json. Create the thin runner scripts/experiments/experiment_8308_v717_sentence_spline_fit.py. Store primitive evidence under results/raw/experiment_8308_v717_sentence_spline_fit/. Read current upstream tasks by their exact declared deliverables; paths not yet produced are dependencies, not historical files.\nCONCRETE STEPS:\n1. PRECONDITIONS: Emit a flushed start line. Authenticate input bytes and terminal/adversarial sidecars. Check private scratch, tools and required resources before measurement. Missing external operands produce complete_blocked_<operand>, verdict_class=blocked and exact gate_check_summary; never substitute simulated observations.\n2. Emit a flushed progress line at every phase boundary and before and after every model load, generation, benchmark and subprocess. Print completed/pending counts inside long loops and a heartbeat at least every 60 seconds while children run; keep every gap below 600 seconds. Use unbuffered output, deadlines and owned process-group cleanup. Write any file over about 200 lines in several tool calls of at most about 150 lines, with a progress message between calls. Split commands and file creation into resumable batches; no single huge tool call and no padded runtime.\n3. Spec first: add relevant REQ-* and SCENARIO-* before implementation. Write focused failing tests first. Preserve existing tests, validators and historical primary bytes. Reuse existing numeric and reporting modules through small adapters. Freeze owned validation argv and private fixture paths. Scratch belongs in /tmp; real runners in scripts/experiments/. No generator-weight updates or external publication.\n4. Declare no_model_load, inference_substrate=verifier_ensemble_against_cached_candidates and MODEL_SPECS=[]. Train small heads only; record trained_head_specs. Read the qualified protocol, custody and kernel artifacts from this roadmap by their declared deliverables.\n5. Fit on128 intended fit sources only. For spline34 use fixed cubic basis from Exp8306 with shared eta=a*x[0]+b+sum(theta*B); compare RBF34 using32 label-blind farthest-point centers on the same four local inputs (start smallest source ID, ties by ID, width=median nonzero center distance, basis_j=exp(-squared_distance/(2*width**2)); fewer than32 distinct fit vectors is insufficient geometry), linear6 with eta=a*x[0]+b+w dot local_features, scalar2 with eta=a*x[0]+b and frozen holistic probability. Equivalent sigmoid34 is an exact re-expression of spline34, not an independent method.\n6. Freeze seed7178308, full-batch logistic loss, 400 steps at learning rate0.01 and L2=.001 applied only during static fitting. Initialize a=1 and all other coefficients0. Project a to[0,2] and other coefficients to[-4,4]. L2 applies to local coefficients and(a-1), not intercept. Record loss, gradient and projected-gradient residual at start/end. If compared optimizers have not converged, scope differences to the frozen training procedures, not geometry alone. No per-arm hyperparameter search. RBF and spline each have34 parameters; report linear/scalar parameter differences.\n7. On the first32 tune slots choose temperature from[.5,1,2] by mean log loss, ties closest to1 then smaller. On the next32 choose the simple comparator among RBF34/linear6/scalar2 by cost, then Brier, then that fixed order. Missing rows escalate for all arms and cost.5; never choose comparator on reserved labels.\n8. Use cost wrong accept=1, wrong reject=1, correct action=0, escalate=.5. Lock acceptance p<.25 and rejection p>.75 with boundary ties escalating; report that these conservative thresholds are a fixed policy, not optimal under this cost. y=1 means unsupported. Freeze fitted parameters, temperatures, selected comparator, role hashes and whole-model hash before reserved evaluation. Before natural measurement, use a separate fit-only constructed control to prove the exact400-step budget reduces loss and changes a typed action. Record initial/final projected-gradient residuals and saturated-logit counts. Failure is complete_null_optimizer_control, not informative evidence against sentence features. Set heads_ready_score on finite trained heads, passed optimizer control and owned checks, never on improved natural fit/tune scores.\n9. Export checkpoint and predictor-only API under results/raw/experiment_8308_v717_sentence_spline_fit/. Mutate labels and source identity in negative tests to prove they cannot reach prediction input. Do not rewrite V713 H1/H2 or invoke model capture.\n10. Run applicable E2E-015 and E2E-019 private source/label fixtures. Run the specified private E2E checks from ops/e2e-test-plan.md and relevant unit/consumer tests. Require 100 percent newly owned statement coverage including real CLI, child, failure and recovery paths. Run scoped Ruff check/format, strict mypy and scripts/check_spec_coverage.py --files <owned-test-files>. Keep exact argv, exit codes, clocks and output hashes. Use pytest -n 0 -o addopts= with private scratch. Do not launch the full repository test suite inside this bounded experiment.\n11. Cold-replay primitive rows in a fresh process, including valid, negative and rehashed-tamper controls. Validate a private candidate with unchanged primary_publication checks, scripts/adversarial_verify.py --json <private-candidate> and scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py --strict <private-candidate>. Publish the terminal primary atomically after normal completion and required checks. Failed owned checks disqualify and set readiness to zero. External incompleteness is blocked, not partial. Reconcile openspec/, _bmad/traceability.md, ops/status.md and ops/changelog.md. Do not modify research-roadmap.yaml.\nREQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:\noptimizer_control_passed, optimization_residuals, saturation_rows: principle: Unreachable actions or unfinished optimization cannot be presented as a representation-level scientific null.\nexperiment_id, task_id, milestone, run_date: principle: Identify the actual invocation and its execution authority.\nhonest_verdict, verdict_class: principle: Terminal honest_verdict starts complete_; verdict_class is positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial. Partial is only retryable unfinished owned work, never an unchanged external block.\ngate_check_summary: principle: Every block names the upstream, actual path/hash, exact field, operator, expected and observed values; absent evidence differs from measured zero.\ninference_substrate, inference_substrate_class, MODEL_SPECS, model_invocation_counts, historical_model_provenance: principle: Separate current model execution from imported observations; do not apply a generation floor to cached scoring.\nrows, intended_count, completed_count, failed_count, censored_count, excluded_count, independent_count, sample_size_budget: principle: Preserve every intended source/condition/arm with numerator and denominator; repetitions are not independent samples.\nverifier_is_oracle, exposure_scope, independent_generalization_score, generalized_learning_benefit_score: principle: Oracle-defined success is circular_positive. Reused cohorts are exposed development; both generalization scores stay zero.\nrequired_checks_passed, flagged_adversarial, acceptance_gates, validation_receipts, terminal_validation_sidecar_path: principle: Readiness requires owned checks and byte-bound validation; it does not require a scientific win.\npreconditions_checked, duration_s, phase_spans, random_seed, reproducibility_checksum, source_artifact_hashes, code_config_hashes, raw_shard_hashes: principle: Bind conclusions to measured work, configuration and replayable evidence.\ncited_upstream_artifacts, field_principles: principle: Name imported fields and hashes and explain every added field's evidentiary purpose.\nheads_ready_score, frozen_head_manifest, selected_comparator, fit_loss_rows, calibration_rows, trained_head_specs, coefficient_counts: principle: Training, calibration and comparator selection use disjoint declared roles.\nsigmoid_equivalence_error, feature_information_parity, checkpoint_hashes: principle: Logistic reparameterization cannot establish a uniquely energy-based advantage.\nRun command: cd {project_root} && PYTHONPATH=python:. PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 .venv/bin/python -u scripts/experiments/experiment_8308_v717_sentence_spline_fit.py --date {date}\nDo NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py."}, {"id": "exp8309-reserved-prediction-seal", "title": "Seal every reserved decision before opening evaluator targets", "phase": 2, "track": "verification", "priority": "high", "requires_gpu": false, "max_turns": 30, "estimated_wall_time_min": 35, "per_unit_rows": true, "milestone": "2026.10.717", "deliverable": "results/experiment_8309_v717_reserved_prediction_seal.json", "inference_substrate_class": "no_model_load", "MODEL_SPECS": [], "gated_on": [{"upstream": "exp8308-sentence-spline-fit", "artifact_field": "heads_ready_score", "op": "==", "value": 1}], "prior_failures": [{"experiment_id": "exp8238-margin-prediction-seal", "verdict": "complete_null_margin_prediction_seal", "addressed_by": "Seal predictions from newly frozen sentence-spline heads without recapturing or tuning an already exposed reserved set. The task measures eligibility, not benefit.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}], "prompt