p every gap below 600 seconds. Use unbuffered output, deadlines and owned process-group cleanup. Write any file over about 200 lines in several tool calls of at most about 150 lines, with a progress message between calls. Split commands and file creation into resumable batches; no single huge tool call and no padded runtime.\n3. Spec first: add relevant REQ-* and SCENARIO-* before implementation. Write focused failing tests first. Preserve existing tests, validators and historical primary bytes. Reuse existing numeric and reporting modules through small adapters. Freeze owned validation argv and private fixture paths. Scratch belongs in /tmp; real runners in scripts/experiments/. No generator-weight updates or external publication.\n4. Use no_model_load, inference_substrate=verifier_ensemble_against_cached_candidates, MODEL_SPECS=[] and zero current LLM calls. Consume only the predictor shards from Exp8305 and frozen head manifest from Exp8308; enforce an allowlist of input fields.\n5. In a fresh child that receives no evaluator shard, score all128 original reserved slots with every fitted arm and the fixed comparator. Preserve97 historical usable feature rows and31 unavailable slots unless authenticated reconstruction explains a discrepancy. Emit missing rows as p=null, action=escalate and unavailable status, never zero probability.\n6. Write source ID, ordered slot, arm, probability, action, feature/head/protocol hash and issue timestamp for each intended row. Create one immutable seal manifest before any evaluator target is opened. Keep stream96 and retention32 in separate predictor-only files; the retention labels remain unavailable to online learning.\n7. Replay prediction bytes and exact sigmoid34 parity independently, then test label injection, changed head hash and changed source bytes. Set predictions_ready_score=1 only on all intended rows accounted for and passed checks. This is exposed-development prediction reconstruction, not a newly blinded external t