nd required resources before measurement. Missing external operands produce complete_blocked_<operand>, verdict_class=blocked and exact gate_check_summary; never substitute simulated observations.\n2. Emit a flushed progress line at every phase boundary and before and after every model load, generation, benchmark and subprocess. Print completed/pending counts inside long loops and a heartbeat at least every 60 seconds while children run; keep every gap below 600 seconds. Use unbuffered output, deadlines and owned process-group cleanup. Write any file over about 200 lines in several tool calls of at most about 150 lines, with a progress message between calls. Split commands and file creation into resumable batches; no single huge tool call and no padded runtime.\n3. Spec first: add relevant REQ-* and SCENARIO-* before implementation. Write focused failing tests first. Preserve existing tests, validators and historical primary bytes. Reuse existing numeric and reporting modules through small adapters. Freeze owned validation argv and private fixture paths. Scratch belongs in /tmp; real runners in scripts/experiments/. No generator-weight updates or external publication.\n4. Declare MODEL_SPECS=[unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF], Q4_K_M, inference_substrate=live_llm_inference and inference_substrate_class=model_bounded_generation. The honest duration floor is10s for this fixed small token budget, not60s full generation. Record planned versus actual class; a block before weights load records no_model_load with zero calls. Never substitute CPU or a smaller headline model.\n5. Authenticate current Exp8307 readiness, lease binding and runtime/library hashes. Acquire the existing exclusive lease, repeat only the immediate context/copy health check and abort on drift before loading. Confirm cache file/hash and GPU memory headroom; preserve unrelated workers. No generator training or driver operations.\n6. Reuse the qualified V714 focal-tokenizer/intervention runner and frozen V713 request semantics. Load Qwen once, CUDA offload required with PID/device memory and layer receipts. Select the first12 label-blind eligible fit sources and at most36 original/selected-deletion/length-controlled deletion requests, max64 output tokens each, temperature0 and seed7138250. Keep answer bytes fixed. No label-driven selection.\n7. Bound load at180 seconds, each request at60 seconds, inference at900 seconds total. Checkpoint after each triplet with progress inside generation polling; preserve all timeouts and intended units. Count model loads, generated tokens and GPU-active telemetry separately from cached prior evidence.\n8. Require >=9 complete triplets, zero custody/cross-talk failures and authenticated live-GPU execution for bounded_canary_ready_score=1; readiness is independent of direction or magnitude of deletion effects. Missing support is a terminal null/block with exact operands, never fabricated completion.\n9. Write docs/research-notes/v717-live-reopen-evidence.md with measured throughput and prospective separate fit/tune/reserved budget estimates. The V713 full study remains parked for a future plan even if this canary passes. These observations cannot augment the current CPU study after its protocol is frozen.\n10. Run applicable E2E-016 and E2E-019 private transport fixtures before live work. Run the specified private E2E checks from ops/e2e-test-plan.md and relevant unit/consumer tests. Require 100 percent newly owned statement coverage including real CLI, child, failure and recovery paths. Run scoped Ruff check/format, strict mypy and scripts/check_spec_coverage.py --files <owned-test-files>. Keep exact argv, exit codes, clocks and output hashes. Use pytest -n 0 -o addopts= with private scratch. Do not launch the full repository test suite inside this bounded experiment.\n11. Cold-replay primitive rows in a fresh process, including valid, negative and rehashed-tamper controls. Validate a private candidate with unchanged primary_publication checks, scripts/adversarial_verify.py --json <private-candidate> and scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py --strict <private-candidate>. Publish the terminal primary atomically after normal completion and required checks. Failed owned checks disqualify and set readiness to zero. External incompleteness is blocked, not partial. Reconcile openspec/, _bmad/traceability.md, ops/status.md and ops/changelog.md. Do not modify research-roadmap.yaml.\nREQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:\nexperiment_id, task_id, milestone, run_date: principle: Identify the actual invocation and its execution authority.\nhonest_verdict, verdict_class: principle: Terminal honest_verdict starts complete_; verdict_class is positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial. Partial is only retryable unfinished owned work, never an unchanged external block.\ngate_check_summary: principle: Every block names the upstream, actual path/hash, exact field, operator, expected and observed values; absent evidence differs from measured zero.\ninference_substrate, inference_substrate_class, MODEL_SPECS, model_invocation_counts, historical_model_provenance: principle: Separate current model execution from imported observations; do not apply a generation floor to cached scoring.\nrows, intended_count, completed_count, failed_count, censored_count, excluded_count, independent_count, sample_size_budget: principle: Preserve every intended source/condition/arm with numerator and denominator; repetitions are not independent samples.\nverifier_is_oracle, exposure_scope, independent_generalization_score, generalized_learning_benefit_score: principle: Oracle-defined success is circular_positive. Reused cohorts are exposed development; both generalization scores stay zero.\nrequired_checks_passed, flagged_adversarial, acceptance_gates, validation_receipts, terminal_validation_sidecar_path: principle: Readiness requires owned checks and byte-bound validation; it does not require a scientific win.\npreconditions_checked, duration_s, phase_spans, random_seed, reproducibility_checksum, source_artifact_hashes, code_config_hashes, raw_shard_hashes: principle: Bind conclusions to measured work, configuration and replayable evidence.\ncited_upstream_artifacts, field_principles: principle: Name imported fields and hashes and explain every added field's evidentiary purpose.\nbounded_canary_ready_score, model_file_sha256, quantization, lease_receipt, live_gpu_receipts, actual_model_load_count, actual_generation_count: principle: Bounded transport readiness requires actual mandated-model GPU work.\nper_source_triplet_rows, request_token_counts, acquisition_cost_rows, future_capture_budget_estimates: principle: A small canary does not establish verification efficacy or authorize outcome-selected data augmentation.\nRun command: cd {project_root} && PYTHONPATH=python:. PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 .venv/bin/python -u scripts/experiments/experiment_8313_v717_changed_runtime_canary.py --date {date}\nDo NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py."}, {"id": "exp8314-arc-coverage-frontier", "title": "Close the ARC reader coverage gap and inspect new supervisor outcomes", "phase": 4, "track": "arc", "priority": "high", "requires_gpu": false, "max_turns": 100, "estimated_wall_time_min": 65, "per_unit_rows": true, "milestone": "2026.10.717", "deliverable": "results/experiment_8314_v717_arc_coverage_frontier.json", "inference_substrate_class": "no_model_load", "MODEL_SPECS": [], "gated_on": [], "prior_failures": [{"experiment_id": "exp8300-arc-outcome-frontier", "verdict": "complete_disqualified_owned_checks", "addressed_by": "V716 measured one unexecuted statement in arc_outcome_execution_8300.py (84/85), after consumer splitting. Add a focused real-path regression for that exact gap and preserve every assertion; more timeout alone cannot fix coverage.", "retire_if_same_verdict": true}, {"experiment_id": "exp8286-arc-outcome-frontier", "verdict": "complete_disqualified_owned_checks", "add