ternal operands produce complete_blocked_<operand>, verdict_class=blocked and exact gate_check_summary; never substitute simulated observations.\n2. Emit a flushed progress line at every phase boundary and before and after every model load, generation, benchmark and subprocess. Print completed/pending counts inside long loops and a heartbeat at least every 60 seconds while children run; keep every gap below 600 seconds. Use unbuffered output, deadlines and owned process-group cleanup. Write any file over about 200 lines in several tool calls of at most about 150 lines, with a progress message between calls. Split commands and file creation into resumable batches; no single huge tool call and no padded runtime.\n3. Spec first: add relevant REQ-* and SCENARIO-* before implementation. Write focused failing tests first. Preserve existing tests, validators and historical primary bytes. Reuse existing numeric and reporting modules through small adapters. Freeze owned validation argv and private fixture paths. Scratch belongs in /tmp; real runners in scripts/experiments/. No generator-weight updates or external publication.\n4. Declare no_model_load, inference_substrate=aggregation_from_upstream_artifacts, MODEL_SPECS=[] and zero current game/model runs. Registry-precheck the existing live solves; this task claims zero new levels and makes no per-game adapter or offline-BFS solve.\n5. Read V716's persisted coverage summary and commands: arc_outcome_execution_8300.py had84/85 statements measured, owned coverage failed, and the unrelated full-suite health probe timed out. Reproduce the missing owned statement under private combined unit/CLI coverage, write its failing regression first, and exercise the real branch. Preserve all prior assertions and100 percent threshold. Do not edit guard/conductor machinery or rerun the full suite.\n6. Use a thin current binding to the qualified frontier reducer after exact coverage qualification. Run the SAME seven affected consumer files l