 measurement. Missing external operands produce complete_blocked_<operand>, verdict_class=blocked and exact gate_check_summary; never substitute simulated observations.\n2. Emit a flushed progress line at every phase boundary and before and after every model load, generation, benchmark and subprocess. Print completed/pending counts inside long loops and a heartbeat at least every 60 seconds while children run; keep every gap below 600 seconds. Use unbuffered output, deadlines and owned process-group cleanup. Write any file over about 200 lines in several tool calls of at most about 150 lines, with a progress message between calls. Split commands and file creation into resumable batches; no single huge tool call and no padded runtime.\n3. Spec first: add relevant REQ-* and SCENARIO-* before implementation. Write focused failing tests first. Preserve existing tests, validators and historical primary bytes. Reuse existing numeric and reporting modules through small adapters. Freeze owned validation argv and private fixture paths. Scratch belongs in /tmp; real runners in scripts/experiments/. No generator-weight updates or external publication.\n4. Declare no_model_load, MODEL_SPECS=[] and zero model calls. Use aggregation_from_upstream_artifacts for imported costs and verifier_ensemble_against_cached_candidates for CPU execution; no hardware_smoke unless an actual board command runs. Run independently of CUDA and positive scientific verdicts.\n5. Read qualified Exp8306 fixture costs and any qualified Exp8310 natural costs as separate branches. Freeze current code/config hashes and replay five alternating full/indexed repetitions after warmup on the same updates. Include basis construction, index lookup/invalidation, gradients, serialization, fsync/acknowledgment, restart work and predictor costs. Do not omit all-cache invalidations or amortize away persistence.\n6. Report paired medians and tail times with unit-level rows; repeats are not independent units. Compare frozen-intercept local updates with full recomputation. A useful CPU efficiency signal requires exact state/action parity and paired complete-transaction median ratio<=.9 on the natural branch; fixture performance is separately circular. Report null if correctness holds but complete work is slower.\n7. Test software fixed-point emulation at signed16-bit coefficients with12 fractional bits and saturating arithmetic, plus float64 reference. Record coefficient/logit error, action flips and overflow. Escalate boundary cases when conservative error intervals cross.25/.75; never claim a hardware result from emulation. Reuse qualified numerical-bound helpers where possible.\n8. Map every measured operation onto authenticated KV260 capabilities with k_max<=5. The deployed Ising overlay does not automatically execute spline updates or persistence; mark unsupported operations on CPU. Compute an ideal Amdahl upper bound only from measured compatible fractions, and mark missing live acquisition spans unavailable. No fitted100x speedup or NFR-01 compliance claim.\n9. Preserve the latest qualified KV260 transcript and synthesis status. If a newly supported workload actually needs a board probe, SSH kria is the precondition with a bounded20-second connection and120-second command; never require host removable storage. Otherwise do not rerun availability. Write docs/research-notes/v717-kv260-local-costs.md with precise terminal obligations and hardware-wishlist implications.\n10. Run applicable E2E-015 private cost inputs; applicable E2E-006 only for an actual compatible board measurement. Run the specified private E2E checks from ops/e2e-test-plan.md and relevant unit/consumer tests. Require 100 percent newly owned statement coverage including real CLI, child, failure and recovery paths. Run scoped Ruff check/format, strict mypy and scripts/check_spec_coverage.py --files <owned-test-files>. Keep exact argv, exit codes, clocks and output hashes. Use pytest -n 0 -o addopts= with privat