e_check_summary; never substitute simulated observations.\n2. Emit a flushed progress line at every phase boundary and before and after every model load, generation, benchmark and subprocess. Print completed/pending counts inside long loops and a heartbeat at least every 60 seconds while children run; keep every gap below 600 seconds. Use unbuffered output, deadlines and owned process-group cleanup. Write any file over about 200 lines in several tool calls of at most about 150 lines, with a progress message between calls. Split commands and file creation into resumable batches; no single huge tool call and no padded runtime.\n3. Spec first: add relevant REQ-* and SCENARIO-* before implementation. Write focused failing tests first. Preserve existing tests, validators and historical primary bytes. Reuse existing numeric and reporting modules through small adapters. Freeze owned validation argv and private fixture paths. Scratch belongs in /tmp; real runners in scripts/experiments/. No generator-weight updates or external publication.\n4. Use no_model_load, inference_substrate=aggregation_from_upstream_artifacts, MODEL_SPECS=[] and zero current model/device calls. Reuse the existing qualified physical-change ledger; no new probing framework.\n5. Authenticate Exp8302's original transcript/hash and operator-evidence frontier. Inspect only cable, port, power or board changes with dated receipts after that frontier. New planning date or rebuilt host bitstream is not changed physical evidence.\n6. Write docs/research-notes/v717-gatemate-obligation.md with one changed/unchanged row, actual evidence paths and an exact reopening condition: documented physical change, authenticated GM1Ax IDCODE, then n16 tile flash and sample/hash smoke. This task makes no JTAG calls, including when a new change is found; a subsequent bring-up plan must name the new evidence.\n7. Emit complete_blocked_gatemate_physical_change, verdict_class=blocked once if unchanged. Set gatemate_obligation_ready_score=1 only for an authenticated obligation ledger and execution_ready_score=0 until terminal hardware evidence exists. Preserve the difference between successful audit and blocked bring-up; never use partial.\n8. Run applicable E2E-018 private authenticated-history cases. Run the specified private E2E checks from ops/e2e-test-plan.md and relevant unit/consumer tests. Require 100 percent newly owned statement coverage including real CLI, child, failure and recovery paths. Run scoped Ruff check/format, strict mypy and scripts/check_spec_coverage.py --files <owned-test-files>. Keep exact argv, exit codes, clocks and output hashes. Use pytest -n 0 -o addopts= with private scratch. Do not launch the full repository test suite inside this bounded experiment.\n9. Cold-replay primitive rows in a fresh process, including valid, negative and rehashed-tamper controls. Validate a private candidate with unchanged primary_publication checks, scripts/adversarial_verify.py --json <private-candidate> and scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py --strict <private-candidate>. Publish the terminal primary atomically after normal completion and required checks. Failed owned checks disqualify and set readiness to zero. External incompleteness is blocked, not partial. Reconcile openspec/, _bmad/traceability.md, ops/status.md and ops/changelog.md. Do not modify research-roadmap.yaml.\nREQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:\nexperiment_id, task_id, milestone, run_date: principle: Identify the actual invocation and its execution authority.\nhonest_verdict, verdict_class: principle: Terminal honest_verdict starts complete_; verdict_class is positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial. Partial is only retryable unfinished owned work, never an unchanged external block.\ngate_check_summary: principle: Every block names the upstream, actual path/hash, exact field, operator, expected and observed values; absent evidence differs from measured zero.\ninference_substrate, inference_substrate_class, MODEL_SPECS, model_invocation_counts, historical_model_provenance: principle: Separate current model execution from imported observations; do not apply a generation floor to cached scoring.\nrows, intended_count, completed_count, failed_count, censored_count, excluded_count, independent_count, sample_size_budget: principle: Preserve every intended source/condition/arm with numerator and denominator; repetitions are not independent samples.\nverifier_is_oracle, exposure_scope, independent_generalization_score, generalized_learning_benefit_score: principle: Oracle-defined success is circular_positive. Reused cohorts are exposed development; both generalization scores stay zero.\nrequired_checks_passed, flagged_adversarial, acceptance_gates, validation_receipts, terminal_validation_sidecar_path: principle: Readiness requires owned checks and byte-bound validation; it does not require a scientific win.\npreconditions_checked, duration_s, phase_spans, random_seed, reproducibility_checksum, source_artifact_hashes, code_config_hashes, raw_shard_hashes: principle: Bind conclusions to measured work, configuration and replayable evidence.\ncited_upstream_artifacts, field_principles: principle: Name imported fields and hashes and explain every added field's evidentiary purpose.\ngatemate_obligation_ready_score, execution_ready_score, gatemate_obligation, physical_change_rows, physical_change_frontier, current_jtag_retry_count: principle: An unchanged hardware blocker stays visible without wasting repeated probes.\nreopen_contract_path, original_transcript_sha256: principle: The next actionable condition is bound to actual hardware evidence.\nRun command: cd {project_root} && PYTHONPATH=python:. PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 .venv/bin/python -u scripts/experiments/experiment_8316_v717_gatemate_obligation.py --date {date}\nDo NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py."}, {"id": "exp8317-capstone", "title": "Reconcile fourteen outcomes and decide local-learning 