nally; no scientific-success gate on this task.\n5. Enumerate exactly Exp8304 through Exp8317, thirteen upstreams plus this capstone. Compare complete YAML task objects with the visible table/JSON contract and canonical digest; authenticate actual activation snapshots separately. For each slot record executed primary, bound conductor pre-gate artifact, absent producer or current reader failure. Never invent a producer verdict for an absent primary.\n6. Independently cold-replay H1/H2, sparse/dense numerical parity, issue/release ordering, crash recovery and all intended denominators from primitive rows. Keep exposed-development signals, constructed circular-positive mechanics, qualified scientific nulls, insufficient support and external blocks distinct. Missing upstream work is blocked, not partial; current owned reader/check failure is disqualified.\n7. Report H1/H2 under the frozen thresholds and descriptive interval scope only. A spline energy is a logistic re-expression of the same basis; no architecture-specific truth or generalization follows. Record whether local sentence inputs or local update handling changed decisions. Retire the precise failed mechanism on another informative null; do not retire an untested hypothesis because CUDA was unavailable.\n8. Reconcile the sole live canary's current load/generation/token counts and imported historical Qwen receipts without double counting. The original V713 source-deletion hypothesis remains parked/unmeasured unless separately executed in a future milestone; a canary is not H1 evidence for this cached study.\n9. Read ARC, KV260 and GateMate outcomes regardless of CPU science. Authenticate Exp8259's primary, terminal/adversarial sidecars, polarfire_workload_validated=true, required_checks_passed=true, flagged_adversarial=false, board dispatch and output parity before preserving PolarFire graduation. Its scope is board-local Linux CPU, not FPGA fabric acceleration. If any operand cannot authenticate, retain an unmet board obligation.\n10. Use exact current same-verdict prior_failures entries with retire_if_same_verdict=true. Record the permanent retirement recommendations in the capstone and reconcile the existing exclusion manifest according to its normal policy without editing enforcement machinery or inventing operator_override authority. Keep GateMate/CUDA unmet obligations separate from forbidden repeated probes.\n11. Run scripts/publication_gate.py --json under bounded child monitoring and retain g1,g2,g3,g4,paper_ready,unmet_gates with output hashes. Write docs/research-notes/v717-outcomes.md with all fourteen dispositions, three PRD gaps and one falsifiable next evidence condition per branch. No external publication.\n12. Capstone audit readiness can be1 while scientific status is null or blocked. If required science artifacts are absent, use complete_blocked_upstream_evidence once. If all science is measured and unsupported hypotheses are null, publish a terminal null synthesis. Do not retry unchanged external missingness.\n13. Run applicable E2E-018 and E2E-021 private authority/audit CLIs. Run the specified private E2E checks from ops/e2e-test-plan.md and relevant unit/consumer tests. Require 100 percent newly owned statement coverage including real CLI, child, failure and recovery paths. Run scoped Ruff check/format, strict mypy and scripts/check_spec_coverage.py --files <owned-test-files>. Keep exact argv, exit codes, clocks and output hashes. Use pytest -n 0 -o addopts= with private scratch. Do not launch the full repository test suite inside this bounded experiment.\n14. Cold-replay primitive rows in a fresh process, including valid, negative and rehashed-tamper controls. Validate a private candidate with unchanged primary_publication checks, scripts/adversarial_verify.py --json <private-candidate> and scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py --strict <private-candidate>. Publish the terminal primary atomically after normal completion and required checks. Faile